quran[7]{c,v,t}:
  3,71,O People of the Book! Why do you confound the truth with falsehood and conceal the truth while you know (it)?
  3,72,"A group among the People of the Book say (to each other): ‘Believe in what has been revealed to the believers (i.e. the Muslims) in the morning and reject it in the evening, so perhaps they may also turn back (from their religion).’"
  3,73,"(They further say:) ‘And do not believe (anyone) except him who follows your religion.’ (O Esteemed Prophet!) Tell (them): ‘Indeed, the only guidance is the guidance of Allah.’ (They also say to their people: ‘Do not believe) that someone could be given (revealed knowledge) similar to what you were given (in the Torah), or that they could use it to argue against you in your Lord’s presence.’ (O Esteemed Prophet!) Reply (to them): ‘Indeed all grace is in the Hand of Allah; He grants it to whom He wills. And Allah is All-Encompassing, All-Knowing.’"
  3,74,"He especially chooses for His mercy whom He pleases, and Allah is the Possessor of Infinite Grace.’"
  3,75,"And among the People of the Book is he who, if you entrust him with a heap of gold, will return it to you (intact). And among them is he who, if you entrust him with a single dinar (i.e. a gold coin), he will not return it to you unless you keep standing over him. That is because they say: ‘There is no obligation upon us regarding Gentiles (non-Jews).’ They attribute lies to Allah, and they know it themselves."
  3,76,"Yes, whoever fulfils his commitments and is conscious (of his duty to Allah), Allah indeed loves those who are God-conscious."
  3,77,"Those who sell Allah’s covenant and their oaths for a little price—there shall be no share for them in the Hereafter. Allah will neither speak to them, nor look at them on the Day of Resurrection, nor will He purify them. There is a painful punishment for them."
